    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test passes. The audit output confirms the new format working end-to-end: `memberId=NSW2616E6609E3` = `NSW` (region) + `26` (FY) + `16E6609E` (HASH8) + `3` (Luhn CHK).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**New logic in one place** \u2014 `model/MemberId.java`:\n- `of(region, registrationDate, telephone, lastName)` builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, reusing `FiscalYear`, `Sha256Hex.prefix`, and `Luhn.checkDigit` (CHK is computed over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`).\n- `regionOf` / `fiscalYearOf` parse the segments back out (stripping any `-<n>` dedup suffix via the fixed FY+HASH8+CHK tail length), so callers read the identity *from* the memberId.\n\n**Owner** (`model/Owner.java`):\n- Replaced the `customer_code` field/column with `member_id`; getter/setter now `getMemberId`/`setMemberId`.\n- Removed `getMembershipNumber`, `getCheckDigit`, and the `getPrimaryIdentifier` migration shim.\n- `getFiscalYear` and `getLocality` now reference the memberId (falling back to live fields only before assignment), and `getRegion`'s doc points at the memberId's REGION segment.\n\n**Assignment** \u2014 renamed `CustomerCodeAssigner` \u2192 `MemberIdAssigner`, delegating formatting to `MemberId` and keeping collision de-duplication (now against existing `memberId`s). Updated the constructor/field wiring in `OwnerRestControllerV1`.\n\n**Audit** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent` now carries `memberId` (via `owner.getMemberId()`); `OwnerCreationAuditLogger` logs `memberId` and drops the removed `membershipNumber`.\n\n**Schema/contract** \u2014 `member_id` column across all four DB schemas; `openapi.yml` replaces `customerCode`/`checkDigit`/`membershipNumber` with `memberId` and updates the `fiscalYear`/`locality` descriptions.\n\nFull suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
